>For Death, grab a big weapon, have magic resistance AND magic
>cancellation, and beat on it until it dies.

Magic resistance (or being undead) *is* mandatory, since Death's touch
attack kills you outright 15% of the time if you do not have magic
resistance and are not undead.  Magic cancellation is irrelevant to
the equation; does not check your cancellation value at all.

This is different to the "touch of death" spell used by powerful wizardly
monsters (e.g. high-order liches, the Wizard), which kills you outright
if a random number from 0 to (monster's level - 1) is greater than 12.
This effect is negated if you are a demon, vortex, golem, or undead
monster, or if you have magic resistance, or if you are hallucinating
("You have an out of body experience.").

